  <comment view="class">Holy Bible (KJV) — the Beblia Holy Bible XML Format, with a schema written for it (bible.xsd) and an excerpt of the King James Version as «data».

The Beblia project publishes over a thousand Bible translations in one simple XML shape: a bible holds its two testaments, a testament its books, a book its chapters, a chapter its verses — each by number (the format never names a book: 1 is Genesis, 19 Psalms, 43 John). The format ships no schema, so bible.xsd describes it, and the excerpt validates against it: the schema is the rulebook, the excerpt a document that follows it.

The data is three of the best-known passages — Genesis 1:1–5 (“In the beginning God created the heaven and the earth”), Psalm 23 (“The LORD is my shepherd”) and John 3:16 — from the King James Version of 1611, which is in the public domain. Only public-domain translations are used here, as many in the collection are still under copyright.

Beside it, EnglishKJBible is the WHOLE King James Bible — 66 books, 31,102 verses, 5 MB — LINKED rather than copied: the design keeps one box that names the file, and opening it reads the file a level at a time (testaments, then books, chapters, verses). Right-click a verse's Open line to feed it into an algorithm; a Run then sends that verse and nothing else.

Source of the format and text: https://github.com/Beblia/Holy-Bible-XML-Format
The full King James file: https://github.com/Beblia/Holy-Bible-XML-Format/blob/master/EnglishKJBible.xml
About the King James Version: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King_James_Version</comment>
